{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-107-1","title":"Psalms 107:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The psalmist exhorts the redeemed, in praising God, to observe his manifold providence, 4 over travellers; 10 over captives; 17 over sick men; 23 over seamen; 33 and in divers varieties of life.</p>\n<p>A.M. 3468. B.C. 536. (Title.)The author of this Psalm is unknown; but it was evidently written to commemorate the return of the Jews from the Babylonian captivity; and it may easily be perceived that it must have been sung in alternate parts, having a double burden, or two intercalary verses often recurring. Bp. Lowth considers it as written \"after the method of the ancient pastorals, where, be the subject of their verse what it will, each swain endeavours to excel the other; and one may perceive their thoughts and expressions gradually to rise upon each other.\" \"No doubt,\" he adds, \"the composition of this Psalm is admirable throughout; and the descriptive part of it adds at least its share of beauty to the whole; but what is most to be admired is its conciseness, and withal the expressiveness of the diction, which strikes the imagination with illimitable elegance. The weary and bewildered traveller--the miserable captive in the dungeon--the sick and dying man--the seaman foundering in a storm--are described in so affecting a manner, that they far exceed any thing of the kind, though never so much laboured.\"</p>\n<p>Give. 106:1; 118:1; 136:1-26; 1Ch 16:34,41; 2Ch 5:13; 7:3,6; 20:21 good. 119:68; Mt 19:17 for his mercy. 103:17; Lu 1:50</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-2","title":"Psalms 107:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Let the. 31:5; 130:8; Ex 15:16; De 15:15; Isa 35:9; 43:1; 44:22; Lu 1:68 Lu 24:21; Ga 3:13; Tit 2:14; 1Pe 1:18,19 from. 106:10; De 7:8; Jer 15:21; 31:11; Mic 4:10; Lu 1:74</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-3","title":"Psalms 107:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>gathered. 106:47; Isa 11:11-16; 43:5,6; 49:12; Jer 29:14; 31:8,10; Eze 36:24 Eze 39:27; Re 5:9 south. Heb. sea.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-4","title":"Psalms 107:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>wandered. 40; Ge 21:14-16; Nu 14:33; De 8:15; 32:10; Job 12:24; Eze 34:6,12 Heb 11:38; Re 12:6 they found.This is the first similitude; in which the Israelites in captivity are compared to travellers in a dreary, uninhabited, and barren desert, spent with hunger and thirst, as well as by the fatigues of the journey.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-5","title":"Psalms 107:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>Jud 15:18,19; 1Sa 30:11,12; Isa 44:12; Jer 14:18; La 2:19 Mr 8:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-6","title":"Psalms 107:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Then. 13,19,28; 50:15; 91:15; Isa 41:17,18; Jer 29:12-14; Ho 5:15 Heb 4:15,16 he delivered. 2Co 1:8-10; 12:8-10; 2Ti 3:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-7","title":"Psalms 107:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>he led. 77:20; 78:52; 136:16; Ezr 8:21-23; Isa 30:21; 35:8-10; 48:17 Isa 49:8-11; 63:13,14; Jer 6:16; 31:9; 2Pe 2:15,21 that they. 4,36; Ne 11:3; Jer 31:24,38-40; 33:10-13; Heb 11:9,10,16; 12:22 Re 21:2-4,10-27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-8","title":"Psalms 107:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Oh that men. 15,21,31; 81:13-16; De 5:29; 32:29; Isa 48:18 praise. 34:3; 92:1,2; 147:1; Isa 63:7 his wonderful. 40:5; 78:4; 111:4; Da 4:2,3; 6:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-9","title":"Psalms 107:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>34:10; 132:15; 146:7; Isa 55:1-3; Jer 31:14,25; Mt 5:6; Lu 1:53 Re 7:16,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-10","title":"Psalms 107:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Such.Here begins the second comparison; in which the state of the captives in Babylon is illustrated by that of prisoners in a dreary dungeon.</p>\n<p>as sit. Job 3:5; Isa 9:2; Mt 4:16; 22:13; Lu 1:79 bound. 105:18; Ex 2:23,24; 2Ch 33:11; Job 36:8,9; La 3:6,7; Ro 6:20,21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-11","title":"Psalms 107:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>Because. 68:6,18; 106:43; Isa 63:10,11; La 3:39-42; 5:15-17 contemned. 73:24; 113:7-9; 119:24; 2Ch 25:15,16; 33:10; Pr 1:25,30,31 1Sa 2:5-8; Isa 5:19; Jer 44:16; Lu 7:30; 16:14; Ac 20:27; Ro 1:28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-12","title":"Psalms 107:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>he brought. Ex 2:23; 5:18,19; Jud 10:16-18; 16:21,30; Ne 9:37; Isa 51:19,20,23 Isa 52:5; La 5:5,6; Lu 15:14-17 and there. 18:40,41; 22:11; 142:4; 2Ki 6:26,27,33; Job 9:13; Isa 63:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-13","title":"Psalms 107:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>6,19,28; 18:6; 116:3-6; Ex 3:7,8; Jud 4:3; 6:6-10; 10:10-18 2Ch 33:12,13,18,19; Jer 31:18-20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-14","title":"Psalms 107:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>brought. 10; 68:6; Job 3:5; 10:21,22; 15:22,30; 19:8; 33:30; 42:10-12 Isa 42:16; 49:9; 60:1-3; Eph 5:8; 1Pe 2:9 brake. 102:20; 105:19,20; 116:16; 146:7; Job 36:8; Isa 61:1; Jer 52:31-34 Zec 9:11,12; Ac 5:19,25; 12:7-10; 16:26-40</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-15","title":"Psalms 107:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>8,21,31; 116:17-19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-16","title":"Psalms 107:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>Jud 16:3; Isa 45:1,2; Mic 2:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-17","title":"Psalms 107:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>Fools.This is the third comparison; the captives being compared to persons in a dangerous malady, as the consequences of their own sins.</p>\n<p>14:1; 92:6; Pr 1:22; 7:7,22 because. 38:1-8; Nu 11:33,34; 12:10-13; 21:5-9; Isa 57:17,18; Jer 2:19 La 3:39</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-18","title":"Psalms 107:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>abhorreth. Job 33:19-22 and they. 9:13; 88:3; Isa 38:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-19","title":"Psalms 107:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>6,13,28; 30:8-12; 34:4-6; 78:34,35; 116:4-8; Jer 33:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-20","title":"Psalms 107:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>He sent. 147:15,19; 2Ki 20:4,5; Mt 8:8 healed. 30:2,3; 103:3,4; 147:3; Nu 21:8,9; Job 33:23-26 delivered. 49:15; 56:13; Job 33:28-30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-21","title":"Psalms 107:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>8,15,31; 66:5; 2Ch 32:25; Lu 17:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-22","title":"Psalms 107:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>sacrifice. 50:14; 116:12,17; Le 7:12; Heb 13:15; 1Pe 2:5,9 declare. 9:11; 73:28; 105:1,2; 118:17; Isa 12:4 rejoicing. Heb. singing.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-23","title":"Psalms 107:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>They.This is the fourth comparison; their captivity was as dangerous and alarming as a dreadful tempest at sea; with a most natural and striking description of which we are here presented.</p>\n<p>go down. 48:7; Eze 27:26; Ac 27:9-28:31; Re 18:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-24","title":"Psalms 107:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>his wonders. 95:5; 104:24-27; Job 38:8-11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-25","title":"Psalms 107:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>he commandeth. 135:7; 148:8; Jon 1:4 raiseth. Heb. maketh to stand. lifteth. 93:3; Mt 8:24; Joh 6:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-26","title":"Psalms 107:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>their soul. 22:14; 119:28; 2Sa 17:10; Isa 13:7; Na 2:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-27","title":"Psalms 107:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>stagger. Job 12:25; Isa 19:14; 29:9 are at their wit's end. Heb. all their wisdom is swallowedup. Job 37:20; Isa 19:3; *marg: Ac 27:15-20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-28","title":"Psalms 107:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>6,13,19; Jon 1:5,6,14; Mt 8:25; Ac 27:23-25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-29","title":"Psalms 107:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>65:7; 89:9; Jon 1:15; Mt 8:26; Mr 4:39-41; Lu 8:23-25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-30","title":"Psalms 107:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>he bringeth. Joh 6:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-31","title":"Psalms 107:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>Oh that men. 8,15,21; 103:2; 105:1; Ho 2:8; Jon 1:16; 2:9; Mic 6:4,5; Ro 1:20,21 2Ti 3:2; Heb 13:15 his wonderful. 71:17; 72:18,19; 77:11,14; 105:2; Re 15:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-32","title":"Psalms 107:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>exalt. 18:46; 46:10; 99:5,9; Ex 15:2; Isa 12:4; 25:1 in the congregation. 22:22,25; 40:9,10; 66:16; 111:1; 119:46; Ac 4:8-12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-33","title":"Psalms 107:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>turneth. 1Ki 17:1-7; Isa 13:19-21; 19:5-10; 34:9,10; 42:15; 44:27; 50:2 Eze 30:12; Joe 1:20; Na 1:4; Zep 2:9,13 water-springs. 1Ki 18:5; Jer 14:3; Am 4:7,8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-34","title":"Psalms 107:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>a fruitful. Ge 13:10,13; 19:25; De 29:23-28; Isa 32:13-15 barrenness. Heb. saltness. Ge 14:3; Eze 47:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-35","title":"Psalms 107:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>turneth. 114:8; Nu 21:16-18; 2Ki 3:16-20; Isa 35:6,7; 41:17-19; 44:3-5 Eze 47:6-12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-36","title":"Psalms 107:36","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>there he. 146:7; Lu 1:53 a city. 7; Ac 17:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-37","title":"Psalms 107:37","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>sow. Isa 37:30; Jer 29:5; 31:5; Eze 28:26; Am 9:13-15 which may. 65:9-13; Ge 26:12; Joe 1:10-12; Hag 1:5,6,10,11; 2:16-19; Zec 8:12 Ac 14:17; 1Co 3:7; 2Co 9:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-38","title":"Psalms 107:38","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":38,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":38},"content":"<p>He blesseth. 128:1-6; Ge 1:28; 9:1; 12:2; 17:16,20; Ex 1:7; De 28:4,11; 30:9 Jer 30:19; Eze 37:26 suffereth. 144:13,14; Ge 30:43; 31:9; Ex 9:3-7; 12:38; De 7:14; Pr 10:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-39","title":"Psalms 107:39","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":39,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":39},"content":"<p>Again.The incidents detailed in these verses, which frequently occur, and mark the superintendence of a benign Providence, and the hand of a just God, appear to be brought forward to illustrate the return of the Israelites from captivity, and the punishment of their oppressors the Babylonians. Wherefore, at last, as in a common chorus, they conclude with exhorting each other to a serious consideration of these things, and to make a proper return to the Almighty.</p>\n<p>they are. 30:6,7; Ge 45:11; Ru 1:20,21; 1Sa 2:5-7; 2Ki 4:8; 8:3; Job 1:10-17 oppression. Ex 1:13,14; 2:23,24; Jud 6:3-6; 2Ki 10:32; 13:7,22; 14:26 2Ch 15:5,6; Jer 51:33,34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-40","title":"Psalms 107:40","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":40,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":40},"content":"<p>poureth. Job 12:21,24; Isa 23:8,9 contempt. 78:66; Ex 8:3,17,24; Jos 10:24-26; Jud 1:6,7; 4:21; 1Sa 5:9; 6:4 1Ki 21:19; 2Ki 9:35-37; Da 4:33; 5:5,6,18-30; Ac 12:23; Re 19:18 causeth. 4; Job 12:24; Jer 13:15-18 wilderness. or, void place.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-41","title":"Psalms 107:41","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>setteth. 113:7,8; Ru 4:14-17; 1Sa 2:8; Es 8:15-17; Job 5:11; 8:7; 11:15-19 Job 42:10-12; Jer 52:31-34; Jas 5:11 from. or, after. maketh. 78:52; 128:6; Ge 23:5-7; 48:11; 1Sa 2:21; Job 21:11; 42:16; Pr 17:6 Isa 49:20-22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-42","title":"Psalms 107:42","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":42,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":42},"content":"<p>righteous. 52:6; 58:10,11; Job 22:19; Isa 66:10,11,14 iniquity. 63:11; 112:10; Ex 11:7; Job 5:15,16; Pr 10:11; Ro 3:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-107-43","title":"Psalms 107:43","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":107,"verseStart":43,"chapterEnd":107,"verseEnd":43},"content":"<p>is wise. 28:5; 64:9; Isa 5:12; Jer 9:12; Da 10:12; Ho 14:9 they shall understand. 50:23; Jer 9:24; Eph 3:18,19</p>"}]}